+## Context
+
+`src/patch.ts` has private helpers (`isObject`, `setOwn`, `clone`) that handle `__proto__` safely and deep-copy values. Merge patch needs the same behaviour.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+- Goals: RFC 7386 semantics; no mutation or sharing; no throwing (every JSON input is valid).
+- Non-goals: generating merge patches; handling non-JSON values (undefined, functions, cycles).
+
+## Decisions
+
+- New `src/merge-patch.ts` implementing the RFC's MergePatch pseudo-code recursively and building a new result. Reuse the helpers by exporting them from `patch.ts` rather than duplicating.
+- Result members are written with `setOwn` so a `__proto__` key stays data. Target members are read only when own (`Object.hasOwn`).
+- Patch members applied to a non-object target start from `{}`; null members are skipped when building nested results (RFC example `{"bb":{"ccc":null}}` -> `{"bb":{}}`).
+- Value `null` in the patch top-level returns `null`, per RFC.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Exporting helpers from `patch.ts` couples modules slightly; acceptable for a small library.
